    ],
    "own_line": true,
    "norm": "Tests that a variable whose prefix marker has no closing suffix is left as-is, while a complete variable later in the same string is still resolved. Template : \"The ${animal jumps over the ${target} ${target}.\" - \"${animal\" is an unterminated prefix, so it is NOT substituted. - The first \"${target}\" after it is consumed as part of the unterminated expression (no suffix found before the second \"${\"), so it is NOT substituted. - The last \"${target}\" is a well-formed variable and IS replaced with \"lazy dog\". Expected : \"The ${animal jumps over the ${target} lazy dog.\""
   }
